# Every service Dockerfile does `COPY . .` in its build stage after already
# copying a correctly npm-ci'd node_modules from the deps stage. Without this
# file, that `COPY . .` also ships the HOST's own node_modules — on Windows,
# any workspace package (e.g. @petrospecial/auth-shared) that was ever
# `npm install`'d directly on the host gets a symlink pointing at an absolute
# Windows path (C:\Users\...), which clobbers the deps stage's correct
# relative symlink and breaks module resolution inside the Linux build stage
# (surfaced as spurious "Cannot find module '@petrospecial/*'" tsc errors).
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
.git
platform-docs
secrets
